{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788472972876780001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"schematic-gleesome-ballpython","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e6811c29ac5101a7563a4f543fb3fac9ec54c02c487eaacc722691e2bac97056","event_uuid":"4e71baa6-557e-4a4a-962e-5fd849772051","position":{"commit_sha":"db286ddb00f5a16bcdb356870ffd1b7a6eac5938","position":"1788470032489544433-4e71baa6-557e-4a4a-962e-5fd849772051"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"39789760f1185b88182cb4a374281a86bdc21e1ff79b259397e57c1d01aea99d","event_uuid":"68840d8b-e1f9-4ce5-b0fe-3e5f3968887a","position":{"commit_sha":"31913acbe424910e4bfcea756e47b6e465ba11f2","position":"1788470069388880941-68840d8b-e1f9-4ce5-b0fe-3e5f3968887a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f88bbb1f80eb22f07860a5924640c9c560ca41017017cbb5b9d4dc581336c1ba","event_uuid":"39c94895-fa12-4cd7-a0a3-e0c68987642b","position":{"commit_sha":"18ee6de6c2a829562159f209200ddc193c04efe5","position":"1788470129220110979-39c94895-fa12-4cd7-a0a3-e0c68987642b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"28274b53c7d1413b44f769ceb6c04a1b5f66a06ee67c9bd02ab3ec0a6ad2d5e4","event_uuid":"5cf5c4fc-acc9-46a6-b373-ed9ff702491b","position":{"commit_sha":"a5cb4db2c1b5b8d443b579bd0dbe9c484208690b","position":"1788470168868527760-5cf5c4fc-acc9-46a6-b373-ed9ff702491b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c0127cb5da8fd8976a0bafdc9c29dc61086543bc35845b571e00c9e64a4daaf7","event_uuid":"46d73101-1a50-4312-b2a5-30f4dd229d59","position":{"commit_sha":"636e6cfdb9eb129b61ca3770bf27ca9cd09cc14a","position":"1788470206355231285-46d73101-1a50-4312-b2a5-30f4dd229d59"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788470032489544433,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"39c94895-fa12-4cd7-a0a3-e0c68987642b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1c52-5e73-4d61-4124"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe prior slices establish a bounded structural index and Terraform-only tool sessions in both review pipelines [rebar:depraved-classless-rooster]. This slice adds optional independent corroboration from HashiCorp's `terraform-config-inspect` when it is already on `PATH`. The audited upstream basis is commit `2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d`: its shallow loader extracts stable top-level metadata with a nil expression context and does not register Terraform filesystem functions, fetch modules, load providers, or run Terraform.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` and expose `corroborate_diagnostic(module, diagnostic, subject, expected=None)` through established Terraform Pass-1 and Pass-2 sessions.\n\n### Closed query and result contract\n\nAccepted diagnostics are:\n\n- `declaration_present`: named variable, output, managed resource, data resource, module call, or required provider.\n- `module_source_equals`: a named module call has the normalized expected literal source.\n- `required_provider_present`: a named provider requirement exists.\n\nAn exact schema-valid entry returns `match` at T1. Missing or unequal entries, absence claims, and unsupported/computed semantics return `abstain`; upstream silence never proves correctness or absence. Results contain only normalized names, classes, positions, and hashes—not descriptions, defaults, constraints, diagnostics, or other upstream literal payloads.\n\n### Hardened execution\n\n- Resolve only the exact `terraform-config-inspect` basename from inherited `PATH`; canonicalize once and reject non-regular/non-executable or repo/snapshot-contained candidates. Invoke its absolute path without a shell using only `--json <snapshot>`; never pass `--after-init`, `--stack`, repository arguments, or shell text.\n- Copy the immutable indexed whole-module bytes into a fresh directory: regular `.tf` and `.tf.json` files only, no symlinks. Make it read-only, run there, and never pass the repository path.\n- Close stdin, create a process group/session, and allow only locale, OS-required process variables, and temporary `HOME`/`TMPDIR`. Strip Terraform/OpenTofu, provider/cloud credential, proxy, plugin, CLI-config, and repository variables.\n- Apply the existing 60-second deadline; cap stdout at 4 MiB and stderr at 64 KiB. On timeout, overflow, cancellation, or error, terminate then kill and reap the whole group and remove the snapshot. Hash the executable before and after; replacement abstains.\n- Record backend, canonical path, SHA-256, discoverable version or `unknown`, invocation profile, snapshot digest, normalized query, outcome, and result digest. Never log child streams or environment values.\n\nValidate stdout against a Rebar-owned schema for the audited JSON fields. Every reported filename must remain inside and name a copied snapshot file. Unknown/malformed shapes, upstream diagnostics, nonzero exit, overflow, path mismatch, binary replacement, or version/schema skew produce one closed abstention with no partial facts. A corroborator can strengthen a positive Pass-1 fact or independently support Pass-2; it cannot originate a finding, veto ordinary review, or turn abstention into negative evidence.\n\n### Pinned upstream canary\n\nExtend the optionality workflow with a gating lane that installs `github.com/hashicorp/terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d`, exposes only that binary on the test `PATH`, and drives the real adapter over a module containing every supported declaration. Assert positive matches, absence-as-abstention, schema acceptance, provenance, and cleanup. Document an identical local command. Normal unit tests remain network-free and substitute an executable fixture only at the process boundary.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nHashiCorp's deliberately shallow extractor provides a narrow authoritative cross-check. A minimal snapshot and fixed process contract prevent repository config, plugins, cached modules, and ambient credentials from affecting it; match-only semantics absorb upstream incompleteness safely.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nTerraform/OpenTofu and provider execution; validate/plan/init/get; TFLint, Trivy, tfparse, terraform-ls, or terraform-docs; module fetch; after-init and stack modes; arbitrary diagnostics; absence claims; expression evaluation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Unit tests through the production adapter prove the closed diagnostic enum and exact-match T1 outcomes for every supported class; missing, unequal, absence-claim, and computed controls return `abstain`.\n- [ ] Parent/child subprocess tests capture argv, cwd, stdin, environment, permissions, and bytes, proving only canonical `terraform-config-inspect --json <snapshot>` launches and no repo path, symlink, credential/config variable, or forbidden executable reaches it.\n- [ ] Timeout, overflow, cancellation, nonzero-exit, and parser-failure fault tests observe process-group reaping and snapshot removal before return; a clean retry succeeds.\n- [ ] Producer/consumer contract tests prove diagnostics, unknown/malformed fields, escaping filenames, changed binary digests, and version/schema skew yield one redacted abstention without partial facts.\n- [ ] Receipt tests assert provenance fields and byte-scan results, receipts, logs, and exceptions to prove fixture literals, credentials, streams, and environment values never escape.\n- [ ] Terraform plan-review and code-review Pass 1/Pass 2 advertise `corroborate_diagnostic`; non-IaC and missing-extra sessions do not, and abstention leaves the ordinary decision path unchanged.\n- [ ] The optionality workflow runs the real adapter against the exact audited commit and fails on drift; `docs/grounding.md` gives the same opt-in local canary.\n- [ ] ADR 0111 records the executable trust boundary, audited commit, match-only semantics, and prohibition on every other Terraform-related executable.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, upstream README/JSON at the pinned commit, and [rebar:depraved-classless-rooster].\n- Preconditions: indexed module; executable fixtures for success, skew, secret-bearing output, overflow, hang, signal-resistant child, and self-replacement; pinned real binary in the canary.\n- Production path: real snapshot, discovery, launcher, bounded capture, schema parser, receipt, and routing; unit tests replace only the executable.\n- Tiers: schema unit, real parent/child subprocess, workflow integration, and live upstream contract canary.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/tier/reason; captured child contract; child absent, snapshot removed, retry successful; exact receipt; byte-level non-disclosure.\n- Negative controls: exact positive matches, nearest absence/inequality abstains, and non-Terraform routes expose no tool.\n- CI: `make test` plus the gating pinned-upstream optionality canary.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py","reason":"hardened PATH discovery, immutable snapshot, bounded subprocess, schema parsing, match-only evidence, and provenance"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py","reason":"expose corroborate_diagnostic through established Terraform-scoped sessions"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/terraform_config_inspect.schema.json","reason":"pin the accepted upstream JSON producer contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py","reason":"query enum, schema, redaction, process containment, cleanup, and fault oracles"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/terraform_config_inspect/","reason":"production-shaped module used by the fake and real upstream contract paths"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","reason":"plan-review Pass-1/Pass-2 visibility and abstention integration"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py","reason":"code-review IaC Pass-1/Pass-2 visibility and abstention integration"},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"install and gate against the exact audited upstream commit"},{"path":"docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md","reason":"record executable trust boundary and sole-allowlist decision"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document optional availability, provenance, abstentions, and local canary"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","1c52-5e73-4d61-4124"],["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["terraform","grounding","corroboration","security","optional"],"ticket_id":"c6ce-4d8d-1c12-47cc","ticket_type":"story","title":"Corroborate Terraform diagnostics with terraform-config-inspect","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py -k \"diagnostic or schema or receipt\"","dd_id":"AC1,AC4,AC5","dd_text":"closed queries, match-only schema consumer, provenance, and byte-level redaction"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py -k \"subprocess or timeout or overflow or cancellation or cleanup\"","dd_id":"AC2,AC3","dd_text":"real child contract, allowlist, process-group reaping, snapshot cleanup, and retry"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k corroborate_diagnostic","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Terraform-only Pass-1/Pass-2 routing and abstention control"},{"command":"go install github.com/hashicorp/terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d && env PATH=\"$(go env GOPATH)/bin:$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" REBAR_TERRAFORM_CONFIG_INSPECT_CANARY=1 python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py -k pinned_upstream_canary","dd_id":"AC7,AC8","dd_text":"real pinned HashiCorp producer contract and documented trust boundary"}]},"source_event_uuids":["4e71baa6-557e-4a4a-962e-5fd849772051","68840d8b-e1f9-4ce5-b0fe-3e5f3968887a","39c94895-fa12-4cd7-a0a3-e0c68987642b","5cf5c4fc-acc9-46a6-b373-ed9ff702491b","46d73101-1a50-4312-b2a5-30f4dd229d59"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788472972876780001,"uuid":"accd3db5-a24d-4473-8a40-073971cd6ef3"}